e,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["elasticsearch","java","search-engine"],"visibility":"public","forks":25807,"open_issues":5586,"watchers":76300,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Hello,\n\nI've set up a minimalistic Test-project using elasticsearch. Via a Java-bean, data is being created (four times via a loop -> four documents should be created) and via another bean my whole existing documents are shown on a webpage (with jsp)\n(The code for the create-Bean and the showAll-Bean is attached).\n\nThe problem is, that my loop creates in average 3 documents and not the wanted 4.\nMy documents always store the following two parameters (just for testing purpose): Time-ID (that is the counter of the loop, so it is always a number between 1 and 4) and the actual timestamp (down to milli-secs).\n\nIm getting a \"true\" by creating on the web page and the created id for the documents four times for creating but in my sense-plugin in chrome browser i see the data only created 3 times.\n\n(I'm also still having the problem, that my array gets out of bounds, if there are more than 10 files, like it is descriped in issue 3051 (https://github.com/elasticsearch/elasticsearch/issues/3051). I'm using elasticsearch 0.90.3)\n## Code:\n\npublic String createESData()\n    {\n        String result = \"\";\n        String data = \"\";\n        Node node = nodeBuilder().clusterName(\"testcluster\").node();\n        Client client = node.client();\n\n```\n    try {\n\n        for (int i=0; i<4; i++)\n        {\n            data = \"{\" +\n                \"\\\"Time-ID\\\": \\\"\" + (i+1) + \"\\\",\" +\n                \"\\\"Timestamp\\\": \\\"\" + Calendar.getInstance().getTimeInMillis() + \"\\\"\" +\n                \"}\";\n\n            IndexResponse response = client.prepareIndex(\"times\", \"time\")\n                    .setSource(data)\n                    .execute()\n                    .actionGet();\n\n            result += (i+1) + \")\\t\\t\" + response.getId() + \"<br />\" + \"\\t\" + \"TRUE\" + \"<br />\";\n        }\n    }\n    catch (Exception ex) {\n        result = \"FEHLER: <br />\" + ex.toString();\n    }\n\n    node.close();\n    return result;\n}\n```\n\npublic String showAll()\n    {\n        String result = \"\";\n\n```\n    Node node = nodeBuilder().clusterName(\"testcluster\").node();\n    Client client = node.client();\n\n    SearchHits sh = client.prepareSearch(\"times\").execute().actionGet().getHits();\n\n    result += \"Anzahl der Dateien: \" + sh.getTotalHits() + \"<br />\";\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < sh.getTotalHits(); i++)\n    {\n        result += \"ID \" + sh.getAt(i).getSource().get(\"Time-ID\") \n                + \": \\t\\t\" + sh.getAt(i).getSource().get(\"Timestamp\")\n                + \"\\t\\t\" + \"(\" + sh.getAt(i).getId() + \")\"\n                + \"<br />\";\n    }\n\n    node.close();\n    return result;\n}\n```\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/3618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/3618/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/29398342","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/3051#issuecomment-29398342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/3051","id":29398342,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5Mzk4MzQy","user":{"login":"rosejn","id":36590,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36590?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rosejn","html_url":"https://github.com/rosejn","fo